<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="68784" href="schedule/2019/spring/HIST/265/68784.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="HIST" href="schedule/2019/spring/HIST.xml">History</subject><course id="265" href="schedule/2019/spring/HIST/265.xml">Science in Western Civ</course></parents><sectionNumber>B  </sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Description:  This is a survey of the history of science in the West over the past 2000 years, with an emphasis on the important role science has come to have in our society.  Topics will include the ancient and medieval astronomy, Galileo and the church, the Scientific Revolution, Darwin and evolution, Einstein and relativity, the atom bomb, the discovery of DNA, the invention of computers, and environmental science.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>156</roomNumber><buildingName>Henry Administration Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Sepkoski" firstName="D">Sepkoski, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>